# Cells place-and-route may not use (LibreLane PNR_EXCLUDED_CELL_FILE).
#
# This is the sky130A default list (open_pdks 8afc8346, the PDK the Tiny Tapeout
# action uses: sky130/openlane/sky130_fd_sc_hd/drc_exclude.cells) plus the
# clkdlybuf4s* delay cells. Those are deliberate delay elements (about 1 ns
# each at the slow corner), but OpenROAD's resizer took clkdlybuf4s25_1 as its
# general-purpose buffer: 457 of them in GitHub run 41340028545, up to twelve
# on the slowest path. Banning them makes it buffer with buf_* instead. Hold
# repair keeps the dlygate4sd* cells it is meant to use.
#
# buf_1 and clkbuf_1 are banned for the same reason: the resizer built its
# fan-out trees from them, and with six to ten loads each one is slow (slews
# of 0.7 to 1.0 ns, about 0.9 ns per stage at the slowest corner). The
# slowest path in GitHub run 41474828936 spent about 6 ns of its 20 ns in
# such chains. Synthesis may still use them; only repair is steered to
# buf_2 and larger.
#
# Regenerate: git -C open_pdks show 8afc8346:sky130/openlane/sky130_fd_sc_hd/drc_exclude.cells,
#             then append the clkdlybuf4s* and buf_1/clkbuf_1 lines below.
